[[Lore:Nahagliiv|Nahagliiv]] was a [[Lore:Dragon|dragon]] whose name means "Fury Burn Wither" in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon Language]].

Nahagliiv was among the dragons to die during the [[Lore:Dragon War|Dragon War]] era, with his remains being gathered by the [[Lore:Dragon Cult|Dragon Cult]] and buried in a dragon mound west of [[Lore:Rorikstead|Rorikstead]]. By {{Year|2E 373}}, local tales still named him as the dragon buried near the town, and the [[Lore:Blades|Blades]] recorded him in their atlas of dragons as being deceased by report.{{ref|name=AOD|{{Cite Book|Atlas of Dragons}}}}

Upon his return, Alduin began the process of resurrecting the many dead dragons buried throughout [[Lore:Skyrim|Skyrim]] in ancient times by the Dragon Cult. Nahagliiv made a reappearance approximately before the reformed Blades unsealed [[Lore:Sky Haven Temple|Sky Haven Temple]],{{ref|name=Rat|[[SR:A Cornered Rat|A Cornered Rat]] quest in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} and attempted to terrorize the town of Rorikstead. The [[Lore:Hero|Last Dragonborn]] slew Nahagliiv and absorbed his soul. Having had his soul devoured by another dovah, Nahagliiv was killed permanently and cannot be raised again.{{ref|name=Skyrim|Events of ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}<noinclude>

